// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6094 Add Sysinternals tooling and driver/UAC detection rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6094
// Pull request author: einlamye
// Change: new rule
// Title: Kernel Driver Service Registered From Suspicious Path
// Sigma ID: e63c949e-af9c-435e-af67-fd840d5af84a
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1543.003, T1068
// Description: Detects creation/modification of a service ImagePath pointing to a .sys driver located in a
//   user-writable or non-standard directory. This is a strong indicator of Bring-Your-Own-
//   Vulnerable-Driver (BYOVD): legitimate drivers load from System32\drivers, whereas attackers drop
//   and register vulnerable/malicious drivers from temp, download or profile paths. Complements the
//   static known-bad name/hash driver_load rules by catching the install step regardless of driver
//   name.
// False positives:
//   - Some legitimate software installs drivers from ProgramData or vendor temp paths; baseline and filter known-good driver paths
// References:
//   - https://www.loldrivers.io/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/8e7b36a9de00c979a098f16eb29c1c22fb63cb4b/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_kernel_driver_service_suspicious_path.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where ((RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Services.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "\\ImagePath" and RegistryValueData endswith ".sys") and (RegistryValueData contains "\\Users\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Temp\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Tmp\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\AppData\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\ProgramData\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Windows\\Temp\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\PerfLogs\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Downloads\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Public\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Windows\\Tasks\\")) and (not(RegistryValueData contains "\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\"))
